  "id": "COMPOUND:19233 - PROTEIN:5673",
  "verbalization": "Trichothecolone is implicated in the pathogenesis of LS174T through a multi-step mechanism involving the target SNU-387. The evidence suggests that Trichothecolone acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn targets LS174T. This pathway is supported by multiple high-scoring connections, with Trichothecolone directly linked to SNU-387, and SNU-387 being a target of several compounds, including sec-Butyl acetate, Npc13565, and (2-Methyl-5-Prop-1-En-2-Ylcyclohex-2-En-1-Yl) Acetate, all of which have a known target of LS174T. The consistent scores across these paths indicate a robust, mechanistically plausible relationship. The involvement of multiple compounds targeting SNU-387 suggests a potential role in the regulation of LS174T, possibly through the modulation of cellular processes that are critical for the survival or function of this cell line. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of SNU-387 as a central mediator in the Trichothecolone–LS174T relationship, with the observed scores reflecting the strength of the mechanistic links.",
